  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Los Angeles Declaration Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Twenty-one countries across the Western Hemisphere launched the Los Angeles Declaration on Migration and Protection (LAD) at the Summit of the Americas in Los Angeles, California in June 2022.  In October 2022, USAID created a website to support information sharing across the 21 endorsing countries, including by proposing to include a special focus on data.  Having a central entry point for information exchange, analyzing existing data sources, and closing existing data collection gaps is important to achieving the objectives the LAD and commitments under global agreements such as the Global Compact for Safe, Regular and Orderly Migration (GCM) and the Agenda 2030 of the United Nations. The overall purpose of this project is to support the LAD-endorsing countries to share migration data, best practices, and to highlight actions to further the implementation of the LAD.</narrative>
  </description>
